    {
      "id": "p0089-b011",
      "kind": "quote",
      "source": {
        "text": "All “determinations” are determination. However, I think depending on the context, (please tell me if this is a dumb idea) it could be put in hiragana or kanji instead of katakana instead? Because it’s literally the same thing here (foreshadowing how she will melt when defeated due to her determination) but its meaning is more in a normal, less conspicuous sense, even though it’s pronounced the same way. So just 決意 [ketsui in kanji] or whatever. 決意 vs ケツイ [ketsui in katakana] IDK if there are other instances of this.",
        "raw": "All \"determinations\" are determination. However, I think depending\non the context, (please tell me if this is a dumb idea) it could be put\nin hiragana or kanji instead of katakana instead? Because it's literally\nthe same thing here (foreshadowing how she will melt when defeated\ndue to her determination) but its meaning is more in a normal, less\nconspicuous sense, even though it's pronounced the same way. So just\n;;R'.@'. [ketsui in kanji] or whatever. ;:R'.@'. vs 'T';J-( [ketsui in katakana]\nIDK if there are other instances of this.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.19287252,
          0.73110714,
          0.66476282,
          0.85207857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.19154925,
          0.73039286,
          0.6660861,
          0.85315
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          33,
          34,
          36,
          37,
          38,
          39,
          40,
          41
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "所有“决心”都是同一种决心。不过，能否按语境改用平假名或汉字，而不是片假名？（若这想法很蠢，请告诉我。）这里字面上指的是同一事物，也在暗示她会因自身的决心，在被击败后融化。但这里用的是更日常、更不显眼的含义，读音却相同。所以写成「決意」之类就好；汉字「決意」与片假名「ケツイ」，都读 ketsui（决心）。我不确定还有没有其他这样的例子。",
        "status": "draft",
